1
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Go for the ultimate spin.

2
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Spider-Man is a action, science fiction film directed by Sam Raimi.

3
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
After being bitten by a genetically altered spider at Oscorp, nerdy but endearing high school student
Peter Parker is endowed with amazing powers to become the superhero known as Spider-Man.

4
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Spider-Man / Peter Parker, played by Tobey Maguire.

5
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Green Goblin / Norman Osborn, played by Willem Dafoe.

6
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Mary Jane Watson, played by Kirsten Dunst.

7
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:20,000
Harry Osborn, played by James Franco.

8
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Ben Parker, played by Cliff Robertson.

9
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:24,000
May Parker, played by Rosemary Harris.

10
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Spider-Man is a 2002 American superhero film based on
the Marvel Comics character Spider-Man.

11
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:28,000
Directed by Sam Raimi from a screenplay by David Koepp, it is the first
installment in Raimi's Spider-Man trilogy (2002–2007).

12
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Produced by Columbia Pictures and Laura Ziskin Productions in association with Marvel Enterprises, it stars
Tobey Maguire, Willem Dafoe, Kirsten Dunst, James Franco, Cliff Robertson, and Rosemary Harris.

13
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:32,000
The plot follows the timid teenager Peter Parker, who gains superhuman
abilities after being bitten by a genetically engineered spider.

14
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:34,000
He adopts the masked persona "Spider-Man" and begins to fight crime in New
York City, facing the malevolent Green Goblin in the process.

15
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Development of a live-action Spider-Man film began in 1975, but stalled
for nearly 25 years due to licensing and financial issues.

16
01:04:32,000 --> 01:04:38,000
Columbia Pictures finally licensed the project for a worldwide release in 1999.

17
01:08:34,000 --> 01:08:40,000
Koepp was hired to create a working screenplay, which was eventually
rewritten by Scott Rosenberg and refined by Alvin Sargent.

18
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Various directors were considered before Raimi was hired in 2000.

19
01:16:38,000 --> 01:16:44,000
Filming took place in Los Angeles and New York City from January to June 2001.

20
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
Danny Elfman composed the musical score, while Sony
Pictures Imageworks handled the visual effects.

21
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
Spider-Man premiered at the Mann Village Theater on April 29, 2002, and was
released in the United States on May 3, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

22
01:28:44,000 --> 01:28:50,000
It was a tremendous commercial success, becoming the first film to reach $100 million in a single
weekend, as well as the most successful film based on a comic book at the time.

23
01:32:46,000 --> 01:32:52,000
With a box office gross of $826 million worldwide against its $139 million budget, it was the highest-grossing
superhero film, the sixth-highest-grossing film overall at the time, and third highest-grossing film of 2002.

24
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
It garnered nominations for Best Sound and Best Visual Effects at the
75th Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

25
01:40:50,000 --> 01:40:56,000
Spider-Man is credited for redefining the modern
superhero genre and the summer blockbuster.

26
01:44:52,000 --> 01:44:58,000
It was followed by two sequels, both directed by Raimi:
Spider-Man 2 (2004) and Spider-Man 3 (2007).

27
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
Maguire and Dafoe later reprised their roles in Spider-Man: No Way Home (2021), which explores the
concept of the multiverse and links the Raimi trilogy to the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

28
01:52:56,000 --> 01:53:02,000
The film explores themes of new york city, adolescence,
photographer, loss of loved one, photography.

29
01:56:58,000 --> 01:57:04,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
